# **The rule block is compared byte for byte.** A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`
# (the default there, and on the Windows CI runner) would rewrite its line endings, and the block
# the binary carries would then differ from the one v20 approved — and from the one every other
# platform ships. Keep the file exactly as committed.
skillmaster-cli/internal/prompt/block.md -text

# **The skill package is built byte for byte from these files.** A Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite their line endings; the archive built there would differ from
# the one CI publishes, and the install document checks a file count that assumes the exact set.
skills/skillmaster/** -text
